      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The historic Hanover Courthouse, pictured on the county seal, served as the venue where Patrick Henry argued the Parson's Cause in 1763.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanover_County%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1953, the Barksdale Theatre opened at the Hanover Tavern, becoming the first professional theatre organization in central Virginia.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanover_County%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Hanover County’s name honors the Electorate of Hanover in Germany, reflecting King George I’s dual role as monarch of Britain and Elector of Hanover.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanover_County%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A local initiative highlights four pillars—history, outdoor recreation, agritourism, and events—to showcase the people, places, and experiences that define Hanover.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
